<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Lesson Summary</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01912</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Lesson Summary</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f3dd98e6-6e0e-460d-8052-a2175304e7e5</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you learned how to:</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>Explain the meaning of the intercepts on a graph of a quadratic function in terms of the situation it represents.</item>
        <item>Explain how the numbers in the factored form of a quadratic expression relate to the intercepts of its graph.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00002">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that helped you reach those goals:</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>7.10.1: Graphs of Linear Equations <list id="list-00003">
            <item>In this activity, you located the <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>- and <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>-intercepts of linear graphs.</item>
          </list></item>

        <item>7.10.2: Quadratic Forms and Their Graphs <list id="list-00004">
            <item>In this activity, you looked at different forms of a quadratic and their graphs and picked out characteristics. These characteristics included <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>- and <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>-intercepts.</item>
            <item>7.10.2: Self-Check</item>
            <item>7.10.2: Additional Resources</item>
          </list></item>

        <item>7.10.3: The <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>X</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>- and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>Y</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>-Intercepts of Quadratic Expressions <list id="list-00005">
            <item>In this activity, you continued looking at different forms and graphs of quadratics and identifying their intercepts. You then made observations about how the graphs and forms are related in helping identify intercepts.</item>
            <item>7.10.3: Self Check</item>
            <item>7.10.3: Additional Resources</item>
          </list></item>

        <item>7.10.4: Using the Standard Form of an Equation to Find the <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>X</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>- and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>Y</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>-Intercepts <list id="list-00006">
            <item>In this activity, you used the standard form of a quadratic equation to find the <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>-intercept and the factored form of the same equation to find the <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>-intercepts.</item>
          </list></item>

      </list>
      <para id="para-00003">After these activities, you completed the following <emphasis>practice:</emphasis></para>
      <list id="list-00007">
        <item>7.10.5: Practice</item>
      </list>
      <section class="checking-in" id="sect-00002" data-platform-hidden="assignable">
        <title>Checking In</title>
        <exercise id="d11f3483-56c8-473f-aa11-048ae1506456" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00004">On a scale of 1 to 5, how confident do you feel about the learning goals of this lesson?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00005">Nice reflection! You learn more when you take the time to reflect on your thinking.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>